  "disposition": "implementation_updated",
  "summary": "Enable native CPU cooperative barriers for fused/tail colors and qualify their substitution with ordered portable dispatches.",
  "regressions": [
    "The unfixed native CPU wrappers diverge at width 33 when consecutive colors share bodies across different lanes, in both Coulomb and twist models.",
    "Ninety-six cases compare separate, tail and fused schedules bitwise, including warmstart and cached deltas, widths 0/1/33/95, batches 1/3 and bias modes 0/1/2.",
    "Run the native scheduling oracle in both debug and optimized builds in CPU CI; retain noalias checks."
  ],
  "differences": [
    "Native arithmetic and GPU barriers are unchanged. force_cpu_coroutines makes the existing barriers effective on the CPU backend even without a workgroup parameter.",
    "TileLang uses ordered launches for native fused/tail work; it retains per-color physics dependencies, without claiming fused launch performance. Ordered scatter versus native cached gather can differ in floating accumulation order and remains subject to full native scene/restart contracts.",
    "CPU and Metal evidence cannot certify Ascend synchronization. All previous source-bound reports become historical until final reconciliation."
  ]
}
